restart command - kills the app. doesn't kill the app and prints warning (unless force argument present) if none of persistence is installed and healthy
info command should report persistence accurately
new command - persistence [info/install/uninstall] [target/all] - will try to install or uninstall or give info on installed (such as where the config is, or what the service name is. each provider has its own method).
in install_all instead of installing all, it should install first that successfull in order of the registry. so systemd should go first, then cron for now. rename the install_all method or create a new one and use that.